name: Order-to-cash assurance
tagline: "The Handbook worked example - orders against payments: Expectations, a Reconciliation, an Alert Rule raising Incidents, collections Cases and a Dashboard"
description: "The worked example every Handbook tutorial builds on. Two CSV feeds dropped in an inbox (orders, payments) land through their own Pipelines as the orders and payments Datasets. Four Expectations check them: amounts are never negative (one per feed), every payment refers to a known order, and no order id arrives twice (read on the open items). The Reconciliation o2c_orders_vs_payments compares the amount of each order against the sum paid for it, one month at a time, at tolerance 0: an unpaid order, an orphan payment, a short payment and a duplicate order each become a Break. The o2c_open_items Job writes one row per order id with its unmatched value and status (paid, paid_late, short_paid, over_paid, unpaid, duplicate_order, orphan_payment); the Alert Rule o2c_unmatched_value raises one Incident per order whose unmatched value is 100 or more, and the Case Rule o2c_collections_case groups the Incidents of one customer into one collections Case. A collections workflow with a write-off approval step ships as a body an administrator applies (config/governance/case-workflow.json): a Space Template carries no governance. The o2c_overview Dashboard shows the unmatched value in total, by status and by customer. Synthetic July 2026 sample files (tools/gen-order-to-cash-data.mjs, with planted defects and their ground truth) land in data/samples - create the Space with loadSamples, or copy them into data/inbox/orders and data/inbox/payments. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition."
minEdition: standard
requiresModules[2]: case-management,ops
icon: heroicons_outline:banknotes
contents[9]: "2 Pipelines + schemas (orders, payments)", "4 Expectations (non-negative amounts, known order, unique order id)", "1 Reconciliation (orders against payments) with its recon.run Job", "1 open-items Job (sql.template)", "1 Alert Rule (one Incident per order with an unmatched value of 100 or more)", "1 Case Rule and its caserule.evaluate Job (one collections Case per customer)", "A collections workflow with a write-off approval step, for an administrator to apply", "3 Datasets, 3 Widgets and the o2c_overview Dashboard", "Synthetic sample files with planted defects"
